# Room 3 — hidden trading defaults

If a default decides **how much money**, **when orders fire**, **flatten/kill**, or **session gates**, it must be said out loud in UI and in chat. Do not let equal-split sizing, silent 1-share fallbacks, or similar sit until the first fill.

When adding execution logic: put the rule on the execution posture / watch book, and tell the user in plain language.

**Size:** Engine-internal. Trading today opens **50% 15m / 30% 5m / 20% 1m**; leftover from quiet TFs diverts to whatever is actually printing. Opening fill reservation is lean (~3/6/5 priors, capped under ~50 combined). At ≥85% match a ticket takes ~80% of its TF slot; watch-book Size $ shows that fire-ready amount while warming. A live 15m can add once. Do **not** dump this as a lecture on the operator screen.

**Same day:** Checkboxes gate **new entries**. Post on → open trades may hold through post. Post off → at RTH close: flatten opens, drop committed maps, **clear the belt** (clean slate for the evening). Always flatten by ~8:00 ET. Overnight flat.

**Belt:** Drop **adds** names — they stay through the trading windows you enabled. Max **15**. × removes one; Clear wipes all. Post off at RTH close also clears the belt. Several names can be in at once. One ticker = one open position at a time (Alpaca is one pile of shares); after that exit it can fire again the same day.

**Orders:** Price off **Alpaca last**, not Yahoo close. Style is **per strategy**: pops (scalp/sniper/impulse, and unnamed 1m) → market; slower setups on any TF → limit. Outside RTH always limit. Kill / day-end flatten uses limit.

**Kill:** FLAT disarms, clears belt, drops committed queues, and flattens open paper positions.
